# Git remotes — GitHub primary, iConnectPlus mirrors, GitLab on demand

## Remotes

| Remote | URL | Role |
|--------|-----|------|
| `origin` | `https://github.com/ronanop/enterprise-erp.git` | **Primary** — fetch + default push |
| `iconnectplus` | `https://github.com/Moksh-CacheDigitech/iConnectPlus.git` | **Always-synced mirror** of origin (real history) |
| `iconnectplus-erp` | `https://github.com/moksh-sharma/iConnectPlus-ERP.git` | **Always-synced owner-only mirror** (rewritten authors) |
| `gitlab` | `https://172.16.200.77/cachedigitech/cache-erp-vapt-31-aug.git` | Mirror — update only on explicit request |

GitHub `origin` is the source of truth.

Local `origin` has **two** push URLs (primary + `iconnectplus`). **`iconnectplus-erp` is not on origin pushurl** — it must be synced with the owner-rewrite script so GitHub Contributors on that repo stay as the owner only.

**`iconnectplus-erp` rules**

- Sync **code/refs only** — never sync collaborators, teams, or GitHub settings from origin.
- Every commit on that remote must show owner: **Moksh Sharma** `<moksh-sharma@users.noreply.github.com>`.
- Always sync via `scripts/sync-iconnectplus-erp.ps1` (rewrites author/committer on a temp branch, then `--force` pushes to `iconnectplus-erp`). Do **not** plain `git push iconnectplus-erp` (that would restore multi-author history).

## When the user asks to push / push to git

1. Push to **origin** (also syncs `iconnectplus` via extra push URL).
2. If the iConnectPlus org mirror did not update, also: `git push iconnectplus HEAD:<branch>`.
3. Sync the personal ERP mirror with the owner rewrite:

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/sync-iconnectplus-erp.ps1
```

4. Do **not** push or sync GitLab unless they also asked to sync GitLab.

```bash
git push -u origin HEAD
# Fallback org mirror:
git push iconnectplus HEAD:<branch>
# Personal owner-only mirror (required on every push-to-git):
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/sync-iconnectplus-erp.ps1
```

## When the user asks to sync iconnectplus / iconnectplus-erp

```bash
git push origin HEAD
git push iconnectplus HEAD:<branch>
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/sync-iconnectplus-erp.ps1
```

## When the user asks to sync gitlab

```bash
git push origin HEAD
git push gitlab HEAD:<branch> --force-with-lease
```

Prefer matching the current branch name. Use `--force-with-lease` / force only when the user intends overwrite (the ERP owner-mirror sync uses `--force` by design).

This GitLab host uses a self-signed cert. Local repo already has `http.https://172.16.200.77/.sslVerify=false`. Auth requires a GitLab username + PAT (or SSH key); do not prompt for passwords in non-interactive sessions — ask the user for a token/URL with credentials if push fails.

## Do not

- Skip syncing `iconnectplus` or `iconnectplus-erp` when pushing to origin / "push to git"
- Plain-push multi-author history to `iconnectplus-erp` (always use `scripts/sync-iconnectplus-erp.ps1`)
- Sync collaborators / GitHub settings onto `iconnectplus-erp`
- Rewrite authors on `origin` or `iconnectplus` unless the user explicitly asks
- Auto-sync GitLab on every GitHub push
- Treat GitLab or either iConnectPlus mirror as primary fetch when the user said "push to git"
- Sync the other direction (GitLab → GitHub, or mirrors → origin) unless the user explicitly asks
